  "defect_observations": [
    "Locators checked in the held Handbook of Mathematical Logic scan (PDF page = printed page + 16): Barwise ch. A.1 sec. 5.4 pp. 43-44 shows the countable conjunction/disjunction formation rule, the reading of the subscripts, Lowenheim-Skolem holding and compactness failing, and the need for an infinitary rule; Makkai ch. A.7 sec. 1 pp. 235-236 shows Karp 1964 as first systematic investigation, Scott 1965 as early account, the Karp/Lopez-Escobar Gentzen-type completeness and the admissible-fragment strengthening; p. 254 shows the L_{omega1 omega} sentence characterizing omega; p. 276 shows Theorem 8.11 (Vaught) and the remark that Scott's isomorphism theorem is a direct consequence. All cited locators supported.",
    "Karp completeness (thm:p02-karp-completeness) and the Karp calculus (def:p02-infinitary-derivation, variants.tex 375-385) remain citation-only; the rule/axiom system is deferred to Karp1964, which is not held. The packet body discloses this as \"Cited only\" (127-132). Not counted against D-P3-009, whose goals require stating, not proving, this boundary.",
